# Data handling (DuckDB / pandas / Parquet)

Adapted from awesome-cursorrules pandas + scikit-learn guide; ORM/Flask advice
removed. Catalog SQL and JSON schemas are normative.

## Prefer

- DuckDB for catalog / interval joins; pandas or pyarrow for tabular transforms.
- Vectorized ops over Python row loops on large frames.
- Validate artifacts against `schemas/*.schema.json` and `sql/*.sql`.
- Write sanitized reports under `reports/inspection/`; inventory via `mbs inspect`.

## Never

- Recursively read or summarize `$MBS_DATA_ROOT`, `$MBS_CACHE_ROOT`,
  `$MBS_SCRATCH_ROOT`, `$MBS_ARTIFACT_ROOT`, or `*.zarr` / `*.h5` / `*.bam` /
  `*.idat` / checkpoint blobs (see `AGENTS.md`).
- Silently clip betas or drop samples during ingestion.
- Depend on private or large real datasets in unit tests—use `tests/fixtures/`.

## Splits and QC

- Study-aware splits for evaluation; document cohort filters in manifests.
- Record genome build, probe/locus hashes, and source IDs in manifests—not as
  model features.
